  "name": "Question 14",
  "problem": "The volume of water in a tank was recorded over time for $25$ minutes, starting from time $t=0$ minutes. The following table shows the volume $V(t)$, in liters, recorded at time $t.$\n\n| $t$ | $0$ | $5$ | $10$ | $15$ | $20$ | $25$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $V(t)$ | $120$ | $150$ | $165$ | $180$ | $215$ | $240$ |\n\nApproximate the rate of change of volume at time $t=5$ using a forward difference approximation. Do not round the answer.\n\nAt $t=5,$ the estimated rate of change is {{field-1}} liters per minute.",
  "worked_solution": "We use the forward difference approximation\n\n$$\n{V}^{\u2032}(t)\u2248\\frac{V(t+h)-V(t)}{h}\n$$\n\nat the point $t=5.$ We choose the step size $h$ to be as small as possible, in this case $h=5.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{V}^{\u2032}(5) & \u2248\\frac{V(5+5)-V(5)}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{V(10)-V(5)}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{165-150}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{5} \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, at $t=5$ the rate of change was approximately $3$ liters per minute.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
